SIENNA models/: third-party files, each byte-identical to its source

The four MLPerf Tiny reference models, the CIFAR-10 sample indices and the image-classification label file come from
MLCommons Tiny, https://github.com/mlcommons/tiny (commit 4addd0fa08d216e20637637874e084895f289da4, checked 2026-10-24),
Copyright MLCommons, licensed under the Apache License 2.0 (LICENSE-Apache-2.0.md, that repository's LICENSE.md). Unmodified.

  pretrainedResnet.tflite       benchmark/training/image_classification/trained_models/pretrainedResnet.tflite
  kws_ref_model_float32.tflite  benchmark/training/keyword_spotting/trained_models/kws_ref_model_float32.tflite
  vww_96_float.tflite           benchmark/training/visual_wake_words/trained_models/vww_96_float.tflite
  ad01_fp32.tflite              benchmark/training/anomaly_detection/trained_models/ad01_fp32.tflite
  perf_samples_idxs.npy         benchmark/training/image_classification/perf_samples_idxs.npy
  y_labels.csv                  benchmark/evaluation/datasets/ic01/y_labels.csv

Not in this directory:

  CIFAR-10 (University of Toronto, https://www.cs.toronto.edu/~kriz/cifar.html; Krizhevsky, "Learning Multiple Layers of
  Features from Tiny Images", 2009): the page states no redistribution license, so it is not committed. fetch_cifar10.sh
  downloads it from that page into data/ (git-ignored); without it the resnet8 model is skipped.

  marvin_617de221_0.wav (the kws model's input clip, benchmark/runner/sd_card/) and normal_id_01_00000000_hist_librosa.bin
  (the ad01 model's input, benchmark/reference_submissions/anomaly_detection/datasets/dcase01/): byte-identical copies are in
  MLCommons Tiny at the commit above (Apache 2.0). They are not committed here; fetch_inputs.sh downloads both into this directory
  (git-ignored) and checks each sha256. Without them the kws and ad01 models are skipped.

## lstm_ecg5000.npz
Trained here by `regression.py --action lstm-model` on ECG5000 (UCR time-series archive, Chen et al. 2015; fetched by models/fetch_ecg5000.sh, not committed). Weights under this directory's license.

## selu_cifar10.npz
Trained here by `regression.py --action selu-model` on CIFAR-10 (Krizhevsky 2009; fetched by models/fetch_cifar10.sh train, not committed): a self-normalizing convnet (Klambauer et al. 2017), 78.6% test top-1. Weights under this directory's license.

